    <briefdescription>
<para>Controls how a <computeroutput><ref refid="classQAccelPlot_1_1LineCurve" kindref="compound">LineCurve</ref></computeroutput> renders gaps in its data. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Accessible via the <computeroutput><ref refid="classQAccelPlot_1_1LineCurve_1a304e3f9be82a9fea7cb84b0c55068d9c" kindref="member">LineCurve::gaps</ref></computeroutput> CONSTANT grouped property, for example <computeroutput>gaps.nanMode: QAccelPlot.NanGapMode.Connect</computeroutput>.</para>
<para>A sample is invalid when its X or Y coordinate is NaN or ±Inf, or is not strictly positive on a log-scale axis. Invalid samples are never drawn as markers, never hit-tested, and are excluded from auto-ranging coordinate by coordinate, regardless of <computeroutput>nanMode</computeroutput>.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="classQAccelPlot_1_1LineCurve" kindref="compound">LineCurve</ref> </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
